            "review_text": "David B\nBruce, Australia1173 contributions\n0\nNothing special\nMay 2026 • Couples\nThe restaurant setting is lovely, nestled against a river with ducks providing entertainment. The food was average. We began with over cooked spring rolls. These were followed by chicken and sticky rice patties. The chicken was tough and the rice was stodgy. Next came battered catfish with tomato sauce. The was the hero of the meal. It was rather good. We also had ordinary fried rice and some steamed vegetables. We finished off with large pieces of dragon fruit. \n\nDrinks were expensive. Beer was about three times standard but it was cold.\nRead more\nWritten May 25, 2026",
