            "review_title": "Review at Ben Nay Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Ludo V\nAntwerp, Belgium948 contributions\n0\nLunch in a beautiful setting\nApr 2024 • Couples\nWe have lunch in Ben Nay. This restaurant is located a bit remote in the wild nature. Once on site it is a revelation. Like stilt houses, half on land and half in the water, there are several gazebos where eight people can enjoy lunch. You feel like you're in a different time here. The brown-colored water of the surrounding canals is almost completely overgrown with water hyacinth. Many Vietnamese must have lived in this way - albeit less luxuriously. I would like to stay here for an hour longer to crack a bottle of wine. We enjoy a 'Set' menu:\n* Leghim Soup with pork\n* Bondweed salad with shrimp, pork\n* Fried check with butter, Lemon sauce\n* Steamed fish with Chinese mushroom\n* Sautéed vegetables with garlic\n* Fried rice with crab\n*Fruits\nThe dishes tasty. Good choice!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nShow original\nWritten May 27, 2024",
