            "review_title": "Review at Ben Nay Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Davidjellis\nLowestoft, United Kingdom10225 contributions\n1\nTasty set menu lunch as part of Cu Chi Tunnels cruise excursion - great local food\nDec 2023 • Solo\nI stopped here for a set menu lunch as part of a cruise ship excursion to the Cu Chi Tunnels, which are a short drive away from the restaurant. The restaurant is located in a delightfully pretty position by a river.\n\nThere was a large number of tables laid out in a covered outside dining area and we were shown to a couple of tables for our tour group. The lunch was a set menu, with papaya salad with prawns, fried basa fillet, grilled chicken and sticky rice, water spinach with garlic, seafood fried rice and fresh fruit to finish. They brought out all the food in two servings, so we all had a choice of dishes to choose from. The meal included a drink and I chose the local Bia Saigon beer, which was nice.\n\nThe grounds were pretty, the service was efficient, and the toilets were clean. Would certainly recommend, based on my experience this time.\nRead more\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten February 1, 2024",
